{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d40f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07c0a-a85e-7163-b151-07f832301ae1"},"sequence":2146,"recorded_at":1780531400004287,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"effad38b-c422-4dbf-8b01-ea09bebc28e3","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"effad38b-c422-4dbf-8b01-ea09bebc28e3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"effad38b-c422-4dbf-8b01-ea09bebc28e3"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Round-3 rework is handed off to review (`to-review`, checklist 26/26).\n\nWhat changed:\n\n- **B1 — equality class censused.** New `TestAppendEventRefusesSameLengthDisagreeingBytes` plants a 1-bit-flip same-length forgery at the digest path through production `AppendEvent`. Under the `!bytes.Equal` → `len != len` mutant it fails with `error = <nil>` (the false-success scenario), while both 15-byte `{\"forged\":true}` vectors stay green under it — proving the old blindness. New battery row N13 plus `TestContentEqualityComparisonsAreCensused`, which pins the class at exactly two sites and fails if a third `bytes.Equal` appears.\n- **B2 — per-session parked channel, as an implementation change.** `SessionSummary` gains `Parked`/`BlockingReason`/`RetryHint`. `ListSessions` returns healthy sessions plus one parked entry per torn session (identity filled from the parked record when it verifies; distinct retry hints for bare directory vs parked record vs torn store), and `Resolve` routes healthy sessions only. Retry table and operator remedy (no delete entry by design; remove `<data-root>/sessions/<session-id>` when no retry heals) are documented in `doc.go` and README. Reviewer probe P5 is now a committed test covering healthy listing, healthy resolution, refused differing retry, and identical-retry heal.\n- **N1/N2 while in there.** Position-0 substitution vector plus N16 row with precision control; member-arm subsumption by `canonicaljson` stated in test comments and outcome instead of presented as gate witnesses.\n\nEvidence: battery 30 applied / 30 killed / 0 survivors (16 narrowing, 10 arm-deletion, 2 census-only, 2 audit-only, controls distinct); `go test ./...` 24/24 green; `-race` green across all 24 packages in 4 groups; vet, Windows vet/build, gofmt, tracecheck (60/98), sessrepo cover 87.2% — all exit 0. Tree `93d4a106` by detached-index write-tree over README plus the 7 sessrepo files; outcome rev3 and battery log attached with task-scoped names; work left uncommitted.","reason":null}}
